WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
Birmingham, 1963.

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:07.860
White clergy call Martin Luther
King's protests unwise and untimely.

3
00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:12.340
King, a Baptist minister, writes
his reply from a jail cell.

4
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:16.370
King and the clergy who criticised
him read the same Bible.

5
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:21.380
So if everyone is equal in God's eyes,
what does that demand of believers,

6
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.280
and why have they disagreed?

7
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:27.740
In this mission, you'll follow King's
campaign from a bus boycott to new civil

8
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:28.930
rights laws.

9
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:34.130
Then you'll meet Joni Eareckson Tada,
paralysed at 17 in a diving accident,

10
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.390
who became a disability advocate.

11
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.390
Your mission: find out what
equal worth demands of believers,

12
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.030
and why they have disagreed.
